330 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 162 0 R
/E (In the modern courtroom, forensic evidence is often treated as the ultimate oracle. Pop culture and the infamous "CSI Effect" have conditioned juries and the public to believe that a single strand of hair, a fingerprint, or a drop of blood is an absolute guarantee of guilt.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 162 0 R
/E (But behind the sterile, closed doors of modern laboratories, the reality is far more fragile. Is forensic science truly infallible, or is the legal system placing blind faith in a flawed concept?)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
332 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 162 0 R
/E (Consider DNA, universally praised as the gold standard of criminal investigations. While the genetic code itself is absolute, the interpretation of it is not.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
