335 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 163 0 R
/T (Similarly, fingerprint analysis long considered foolproof relies heavily on human judgment rather than pure mathematics. It is not just algorithms matching exact patterns; it involves human analysts who are naturally susceptible to "cognitive bias." If an analyst is informed that a suspect has a highly violent history, their brain may subconsciously force a pattern match where none actually exists.)
/E (Similarly, fingerprint analysis long considered foolproof relies heavily on human judgment rather than pure mathematics. It is not just algorithms matching exact patterns; it involves human analysts who are naturally susceptible to "cognitive bias." If an analyst is informed that a suspect has a highly violent history, their brain may subconsciously force a pattern match where none actually exists.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
