/E (Similarly, fingerprint analysis long considered foolproof relies heavily on human judgment rather than pure mathematics. It is not just algorithms matching exact patterns; it involves human analysts who are naturally susceptible to "cognitive bias." If an analyst is informed that a suspect has a highly violent history, their brain may subconsciously force a pattern match where none actually exists.)
