<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 169 0 R
/E ( The shifting frontiers of Life: Genetic modification puts into question our traditional concept of what is "Natural & forces us to consider fundamental questions about our own agency in determining the destiny of life here on earth. Open discussion between scientists, ethicists, decision-makers & Citizens is required in addressing these complex philosophical & societal concerns & in creating responsible standards for working with this powerful technology.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
400 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 169 0 R
/E (In conclusion, Genetic Technology is no longer a distant prospect but an evolving reality that is reshaping life's script. From healing debilitating disorders to creating robust food systems & building a tomorrow that is sustainable its capacity for all humanity is immense. But all such potential comes along with a need for wisdom. While we continue to unravel the code of life & continue perfecting our art at code-manipulation, a thoughtful & ethical reaction is called for. By accepting change & examining the social & environmental consequences cautiously, we can see that the BioTech Revolution" weaves a future in which genetic engineering's strands are interwoven in the well-being of all life upon our earth.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
