810 0 obj
<<
/Title (Similarly, fingerprint analysis long considered foolproof relies heavily on human judgment rather than pure mathematics. It is not just algorithms matching exact patterns; it involves human analysts who are naturally susceptible to "cognitive bias." If an analyst is informed that a suspect has a highly violent history, their brain may subconsciously force a pattern match where none actually exists.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 517 0 R
/Next 1018 0 R
>>
endobj
811 0 obj
<<
/Title (Ultimately, forensic science is a powerful tool, not a crystal ball. It is an evolving, imperfect discipline governed by human beings, and humans inevitably make mistakes. For the modern legal system to be truly just, we must strip away the illusion of forensic perfection. We must constantly question the science, rigorously challenge the methods in court, and remember that in the pursuit of justice, blind faith is the greatest enemy of truth.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 517 0 R
/Prev 1019 0 R
>>
endobj
